.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
.\" Hand-written (the monitor has no clap definitions): what the engine
.\" starts it with, not what a user types.
.TH VELARX-MONITOR 8 "" "velarx" "Velarx"
.SH NAME
velarx\-monitor \- the process that owns one container
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B velarx\-monitor
.B \-\-varlink\-fd
.IR N
.IR RUNDIR
.br
.B velarx\-monitor
.B \-\-image\-server
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B velarx\-monitor
is started by the engine
.RB ( velarx (1),
or the engine service of
.BR velarx\-api (8)),
never by a user: it runs one container of the store, from all that the
engine left in
.IR RUNDIR ,
its run directory under the state directory of the engine
.RB ( \-\-runroot ,
.I state_dir
of
.BR velarx.conf (5)).
It is the parent of the init process of the container: it creates the
cgroup of the container and its own below it
.RB ( \-\-cgroups=disabled
asks for none), starts the OCI runtime
.RB ( \-\-runtime ,
.I runtime
of
.BR velarx.conf (5))
with
.B create
and
.BR start ,
follows the exit of the container (and of the processes it reaped), keeps
its log pipe, runs the restart policy, its health checks and the OCI hooks,
and serves
.B org.velarx.Monitor
.RI ( interfaces/org.velarx.Monitor.varlink )
on the monitor socket of the run directory: the engine and
.B "velarx healthcheck"
call it there.
.PP
.I N
is the descriptor of the first connection, which the engine hands the
monitor (nothing is implied: the number is named).  Its first call is
.B Create
(create the container, or restore it from the directory of images that the
call carries as a descriptor); the other descriptors the monitor was passed
are named in
.BR monitor.json .
.B \-\-image\-server
makes the binary the server of the layers of an image for the driver, not a
monitor.
The calls
.BR GetInfo ,
.BR GetCoreStatus ,
.BR Stop ,
.B Kill
and
.B Wait
(the core) mean the same in every version of the monitor, so that the engine
of a newer version still stops a container that an older one started.
.PP
Before the container is created the monitor mounts its root file system and
the images mounted in it from the EROFS images of their layers.  It measures
each image through the descriptor it mounts and refuses one whose fs\-verity
digest is none of the values the engine wrote for that layer in
.B monitor.json
(taken, at that start, from the checked manifest of the image; the bundle's
.B rootfs.json
holds paths only).  When the engine enforces the digests the overlay has
.BR verity=require ,
and an image without fs\-verity is an error.  A restart of the container by
the monitor finds the file systems mounted and checks nothing again.
.PP
With no engine service
.RB ( velarx\ run\ \-\-no\-monitor )
the container runs in the process of the command and there is no monitor.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.I RUNDIR
The run directory of the container: its settings, its sockets and its
files, which the engine made.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and the commit of the build.
.SH EXIT STATUS
The exit status of the init process of the container; 1 when the monitor
itself failed (its error is on the standard error), 2 when it was not
given exactly one
.IR RUNDIR .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR velarx (1),
.BR velarx.conf (5),
.BR crun (1)
